                        "entry_id": "257e1d29-6026-3612-9074-225d6363913e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who papalizes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0ecfa314-5ed6-4466-a9d9-b0768b3118d0",
                                "sense_id": "c0d5a39e-3fac-3593-9475-db115093d357",
                                "text": "Besides, I have as much reason to suspect that what you quote from them was interpolated by Judaizers, as you have to suspect that what I quote from them, was interpolated by papalizers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9ffde72-eaca-4042-be07-cf2fd427b758",
                                "sense_id": "c0d5a39e-3fac-3593-9475-db115093d357",
                                "text": "He was a papalizer of the church in Germany, but that was because he was a missionary, and Rome was the acknowledged and worthy centre of missionary enterprise."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "091a6b6c-d070-4e4b-9c32-9468061ef840",
                                "sense_id": "c0d5a39e-3fac-3593-9475-db115093d357",
                                "text": "When I say papalizers, or the like, call to your mind that such men have all sworn to their King’s religious supremacy. True papists, acknowledging Rome openly, are hard to be found."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
